# Error test (eu-oaz72.43): a negative index to `nth` is reported as a
# negative index. It used to count down past zero until the list ran out —
# forever on an infinite list. A finite list keeps this test bounded if the
# fix regresses: the old code reports "out of range for list of length 3"
# instead, which fails the expected stderr.
x: [1, 2, 3] nth(-1)
